ne  we're looking for autograph cards we are  looking for rookie cards  let's see what we got there may be 12  different  individuals who buy into that and  somebody will break which means open up  the box  in front of a large audience of people  on the internet  and you get the experience of seeing  what you won out of the packs  oh there's a throwback mike piazza  it makes it affordable so that many  people can participate it makes it  social because everybody's rooting for  everybody to get the good cards  it's also a bit like sports betting but  whether that's something  is a hundred dollars or a hundred  thousand you don't know until it's open  my favorite item and my most valuable  item  is a bat that was used by babe ruth  i wouldn't want to put a value on it  except to say it's over a million  dollars  i'd always been someone who dealt in  vintage cards but a new phenomenon that  i noticed that there was this  revolution happening because the younger  generation they wanted to collect  cards of people they grew up with and  they wanted to collect cards  of people that were popular now ronaldo  rookie card  soccer is exploding he is the number one  rookie card to have in soccer right now  we famously sold a lebron james card  for 1.8 million dollars very recently  we sold a kobe bryant card for  approximately 1.79 million dollars  pristine baby kobe bryant pristine  chrome refractor should be looking at  about half a million on this  i've always considered myself a small  business and a small business owner  being able to interact they'll send me a  picture hey you know i've got this ball  what is this worth  i've got this card what do you think  this kobe's worth i answer every single  solitary message and when i wake up in  the morning  there's uh you know dozens more and no  matter how large golden gets  you know i at least i'm always going to  look at it as my small business  trading cards really when you think  about it they're part of society  and they 